Oh, Klaus, did you bring my watch, then? [p]
[freeimage layer=2]
[chara_mod name="Klaus" storage="/chara/2/klaus_closed.png" time=200 cross=false]
#<font face="earthorbiter"><font color="#cc66ff">Klaus</font>
...Good thing you just reminded me, otherwise I probably would have forgotten to give it to you again. [p]

[freeimage layer=1]
[current layer="message1"]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=true]

#<font face="earthorbiter"></font>
Klaus hands the foreign tool over to me. [l]It's really similar to a smartwatch, but with discernible speakers. [l]It also has a small hole just below the screen, which is probably the microphone. [p]
There's only one button on the side, used to power the watch on or off, and a cable entry to charge it. [l]Using such a tool is the logical answer, considering your phone service is useless in space. [p]

[current layer="message0"]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=true]
[image storage=default/UI_Elements/stellar_ui_chat2big.png layer=1 x=35 y=458 visible=true time=0 width=181 height=217]

[chara_mod name="Klaus" storage="/chara/2/klaus.png" time=200 cross=false]
#<font face="earthorbiter"><font color="#cc66ff">Klaus</font>
To turn the screen on, simply double tap on the screen. [p]

[freeimage layer=1]
[current layer="message1"]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=true]

#<font face="earthorbiter"></font>
I follow his advice. [l]As I do, the interface of the screen softly displays like a high end smartphone home screen. [p]

[current layer="message0"]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=true]
[image storage=default/UI_Elements/stellar_ui_chat2big.png layer=1 x=35 y=458 visible=true time=0 width=181 height=217]
[image storage=default/EuphieSprites/euphie_normal_neutral.png layer=2 x=35 y=458 visible=true time=0 width=181 height=217]
#<font face="earthorbiter"><font color="#ff8080">Euphie</font>
And it's... [l]One thirty in the afternoon. [l]Cool. [p]
[freeimage layer=2]
#<font face="earthorbiter"><font color="#cc66ff">Klaus</font>
Of course, it does more than simply display the current time. [p]
By touching the clock, you can check out what time it is down on earth from different time zones, call anyone of us onboard, and most importantly for now, an entirely detailed 3D map of the station. [p]
[freeimage layer=1]

[current layer="message1"]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=true]

#<font face="earthorbiter"></font>
Intrigued, I tap down on the application displaying the map of the place. [p]

[current layer="message0"]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=true]
[image storage=default/UI_Elements/stellar_ui_chat2big.png layer=1 x=35 y=458 visible=true time=0 width=181 height=217]
[image storage=default/EuphieSprites/euphie_normal_speak.png layer=2 x=35 y=458 visible=true time=0 width=181 height=217]
